name: sim.launchExecutable
description: Launches an executable. Similar to os.execute or io.popen, but is system independent.
luaSynopsis: sim.launchExecutable(string filename, string parameters = '', int showStatus = 1)
pythonSynopsis: sim.launchExecutable(string filename, string parameters = '', int showStatus = 1)
inputs:
1. filename: file name of the executable. If the filename starts with '@', then it will be considered as a system command, otherwise the current directory might be automatically prepended to the filename if it makes sense.
2. parameters: optional input arguments
3. showStatus: 0 to hide the application's window, 1 to show it. Works only with Windows OS.
outputs:
